A `--set` on a nested key merges into its mapping rather than replacing it: the overridden key moves
and its siblings under `core.sprint` are still there to render. The sibling is probed for
non-emptiness, not for its size, so growing the scale table does not touch this case.

-- fixtures/cwd/probe.md.j2 --
threshold {{ config.core.sprint.default_threshold_sp }}
scale populated {{ config.core.sprint.scale | length > 0 }}
redecompose {{ config.core.sprint.redecompose_threshold }}
-- cmd --
booping render /proc/self/cwd/probe.md.j2 --set core.sprint.default_threshold_sp=7
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
threshold 7
scale populated True
redecompose 5
-- stderr --
